{"name":"A Pair of Brown Eyes","hex":"#bfaf92","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Two alike or identical things taken together; often followed by of.","One of the constituent items that make up a pair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To group into one or more sets of two.","to link two electronic devices wirelessly together, especially through a protocol such as Bluetooth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pair"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"eyes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of eye"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of eye"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Pair of Brown Eyes","blocks":[{"text":"\"A Pair of Brown Eyes\" is a single by The Pogues, released on 18 March 1985. It featured on the band's second album, Rum Sodomy & the Lash, and was composed by Pogues front man Shane MacGowan. The single was their first to make the UK Top 100, peaking at Number 72. The Los Angeles Times listed it among \"The 10 Essential Shane MacGowan Songs.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Pair_of_Brown_Eyes"},{"title":"Eye color","blocks":[{"text":"Eye color is a polygenic phenotypic trait determined by two factors: the pigmentation of the eye's iris and the frequency-dependence of the scattering of light by the turbid medium in the stroma of the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg/330px-Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_color"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg/500px-Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg/1280px-Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg/500px-Close-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dark brown iris bordering on black","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClose-up_photograph_of_the_eye_of_a_baby_with_reflection_of_the_scene_in_the_pupil_-_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MyStrangeIris.JPG/500px-MyStrangeIris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/MyStrangeIris.JPG/500px-MyStrangeIris.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A light brown iris","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMyStrangeIris.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg/500px-Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg/1280px-Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg/500px-Human_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A light brown iris with limbal ring","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_eye%2C_anterior_view.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Amber_eyes.JPG/500px-Amber_eyes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Amber_eyes.JPG/500px-Amber_eyes.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golden, or amber colored hazel eyes. The iris is the color of a hazelnut shell. This is what hazel eyes traditionally refer to.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmber_eyes.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Hazel_Eye_HD.JPG/500px-Hazel_Eye_HD.J